help.a.templates_variables:
In the template editor (Settings → Templates) the following are available:
• {{anrede}} — Mr / Ms
• {{vorname}}, {{nachname}}, {{firma}}
• {{anlage_name}}, {{mastr_nummer}}, {{kwp}}
• {{ort}}, {{plz}}
• {{owner_signature}} — automatic owner signature

Variables are substituted at send time. In preview you see sample data.

help.a.webhooks_events:
Every webhook payload has this envelope:

```json
{
  "event": "lead.created",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-02T18:42:11.000Z",
  "delivery_id": "a3f2…",
  "data": { … event-specific fields … }
}
```

`data` contains ID + relevant fields (e.g. for `anlage.status_changed`: `anlage_id`, `mastr_nummer`, `old_status`, `new_status`, `changed_by`). Example payloads in the OpenAPI spec.

help.a.webhooks_signature:
Every request carries the header `X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=<hex>`. Compute HMAC-SHA256 over the raw body using the `secret` you received once on creation (format `whsec_…`). Compare in constant time. Example (Node.js):

```js
const crypto = require('crypto');
const expected = 'sha256=' + crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(rawBody).digest('hex');
crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(received), Buffer.from(expected));
```

